<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7202" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναπίπτω</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμπ-</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fall back,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1599
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				410
			</span></i>; <i>lay oneself back,</i>
			like rowers, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				345
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				8.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ὑπτία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					254b
				</span></i>
			, cf. e; of riders, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπτίους ἀναπεπτωκότας ἐλαύνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.Mag.</u>
					3.14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>fall back, give ground,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.70
			</span></i>; <i>flag, lose heart,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.224
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς σπουδαῖς</span> (vulg.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπονδ-</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> ἀναπεπτωκέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					5.53
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			pf.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναπεπτωκώς</span>
			<i>lifeless,</i> of style, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σχῆμα ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					2p.518S.
				</span></i>
			, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of a plan,
				<i>to be given up,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεπεπτώκει τὰ τῆς ἐξόδου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.163
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀπ᾽ οἴκων</span>
			<i>to be banished</i> from one's house, Poet. ap.
				Athenagoras<i>pro Christo</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				22
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>recline</i> at meals, 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάκειμαι</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				293
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				638
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPar.</u>
				51.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Marc.</u>
				6.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Asin.</u>
				23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>take to one's bed</i> in sickness, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Leid.V.</u>
				11.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			<i>recoil,</i> of the arms of torsion-engines, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Bel.</u>
				100.2
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
